# ─── Datasets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ai/datasets/raw/*.csv
ai/datasets/raw/*.tsv
ai/datasets/raw/*.json
ai/datasets/processed/*.csv
ai/datasets/processed/*.json
# Recursive, not just the top level: campaign_snapshots/ (Sprint 4, WBS 4.3.8)
# holds archived clustering runs, and each cluster entry carries a `sample` of
# real message text. A bare `processed/*.json` does not match a subdirectory,
# so archived snapshots would otherwise be committed.
ai/datasets/processed/**/*.json
# Cached embeddings (Sprint 3 clustering). The .npz bundles the message texts
# alongside the vectors -- real personal SMS, same reason as the CSVs. Also
# large and fully regenerable via scripts/embed_dataset.py.
ai/datasets/processed/*.npz

# Raw source corpora + generated labeled data (real personal SMS — never push).
# sample.csv (format reference) and the *.md guides stay tracked.
ai/datasets/bantAI-datasets/
ai/datasets/labeled/*.csv
!ai/datasets/labeled/sample.csv
ai/datasets/audit/

# Dated backups of bantai_labeled.csv taken outside create_holdout_set.py's own
# backup mechanism (which already writes its dated backups directly beside the
# file, no trailing .csv, matching the pattern below at line ~92). Kept OUTSIDE
# ai/datasets/labeled/ on purpose -- both training/dataset.py and
# retraining/snapshot.py glob ai/datasets/labeled/*.csv indiscriminately, so a
# same-directory backup silently doubles the training pool (found 2026-08-26:
# a backup here inflated a local dry-run's row count from 21,571 to 35,107).
ai/datasets/labeled_backups/

# Admin-validated user report exports feeding retraining (Sprint 4, WBS 4.3.5).
# These are real reported SMS bodies -- same reason as the labeled data. The
# README documenting the export format stays tracked.
ai/datasets/reports/*.csv
ai/datasets/reports/*.json
ai/datasets/reports/*.jsonl

# Permanent held-out test set (Sprint 6, WBS 6.4.6 prep -- scripts/create_holdout_set.py).
# Real SMS bodies, same reason as the labeled data above. manifest.json (seed,
# counts, a hash of the CSV -- no message text) stays tracked so the team can
# see a holdout exists and verify it hasn't drifted, without the raw text ever
# being committed. The dated pre-split backup of bantai_labeled.csv the script
# writes matches this pattern too (it ends in the timestamp, not `.csv`).
ai/datasets/holdout/*.csv
ai/datasets/labeled/*.pre-holdout-backup-*

# Colab upload package embeds a full copy of the labeled dataset (real personal
# SMS) inside the zip -- same reason it must never be pushed. Notebook + README
# stay tracked.
ai/colab/*.zip

# Trained model artifacts (1GB+ binaries, regenerable via training/train.py).
ai/models/*/

